    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d157-a1-a4">

                <pb facs="0364" n="344" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg344"/>

                <head>Mr Fessenden to Mr
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Department,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-09-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 30, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of this date transmitting telegram from General Hitchcock, and to
                    state that this department has this day chartered the steam propeller Hector,
                    (at Oswego, New York, ) for revenue cutter purposes. This vessel, together with
                    the Winslow, chartered at Buffalo a few days since, will be fitted for service
                    with all possible despatch, The telegram is herewith returned.</p>
                <p>I am, very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. P. FESSENDEN, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                        Treasury.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
